}, {"rights": {"0": "privileges", "1": "entitlements"}}, {"revive": {"0": "renew", "1": "resurrect"}}, {"their": {"0": "their", "1": "their"}}, {"cultures": {"0": "heritages", "1": "traditions"}}, {"and": {"0": "and", "1": "and"}}, {"reclaim": {"0": "recoup", "1": "retrieve"}}, {"their": {"0": "their", "1": "their"}}, {"lands": {"0": "territories", "1": "properties"}}, {"It": {"0": "It", "1": "It"}}, {"is": {"0": "is", "1": "is"}}, {"imperative": {"0": "crucial", "1": "essential"}}, {"that": {"0": "that", "1": "that"}}, {"we": {"0": "we", "1": "we"}}, {"acknowledge": {"0": "recognize", "1": "admit"}}, {"this": {"0": "this", "1": "this"}}, {"historical": {"0": "historical", "1": "historical"}}, {"injustice": {"0": "wrong", "1": "inequity"}}, {"and": {"0": "and", "1": "and"}}, {"work": {"0": "strive", "1": "labor"}}, {"towards": {"0": "toward", "1": "in the direction of"}}, {"creating": {"0": "building", "1": "developing"}}, {"a": {"0": "a", "1": "a"}}, {"more": {"0": "more", "1": "more"}}, {"equitable": {"0": "fair", "1": "just"}}, {"and": {"0": "and", "1": "and"}}, {"inclusive": {"00": "comprehensive", "01": "integrative", "10": "embracing", "11": "all-encompassing"}}, {"world": {"000": "globe", "001": "earth", "010": "planet", "011": "universe", "100": "realm", "101": "cosmos", "110": "creation", "111": "nature"}}, {"for": {"00": "toward", "01": "to", "10": "in support of", "11": "benefiting"}}, {"all": {"00": "everyone", "01": "everybody", "10": "all people", "11": "each one"}}], "container": "Colonialism had a profound and long-lasting impact on indigenous peoples around the world. The arrival of colonizers resulted in the displacement and marginalization of these communities. Their lands were taken away, and they were subjected to cultural assimilation and discrimination. Indigenous economies were disrupted and traditional ways of life eroded. Additionally, diseases brought by the colonizers decimated indigenous populations. The effects of colonialism continue to be felt today, as indigenous peoples struggle to regain their rights, revive their cultures, and reclaim their lands. It is imperative that we acknowledge this historical injustice and work towards creating a more equitable and inclusive world for all.", "encoded_message": "Colonization experienced a deep as well as lasting bearing upon autochthonous populations surrounding the globe. The coming of settlers caused in the eviction and peripheralization of these groups. Their regions were confiscated away, and they were exposed to civilizational incorporation and prejudice. Aboriginal financial systems were destabilized and customary methods of existence undermined. Moreover, illnesses introduced by the conquerors devastated native peoples. The consequences of colonization persevere to be experienced nowadays, as aboriginal communities fight to recover their privileges, renew their traditions, and retrieve their properties. It is crucial that we acknowledge this historical injustice and work towards creating a more equitable and inclusive world for all.", "encoding_time_report": {"container_generation": 4.05, "secret_key_generation": 98.23}, "decoding_time": 0.0004489421844482422, "decoded_message": "1010000101101000010100001101110110011000010010100010001100001110", "error_message": ""}